         "id": "v2-1cf69-p14-practice-slot-3-124656-slot-3-q-a",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "a",
         "prompt": "$\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\theta\\right)=3\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\theta\\right)$",
         "answerSpaceMm": 80,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=\\frac{7\\pi}{12},\\frac{11\\pi}{12}$",
          "worked": "Let $t=\\tan\\theta$. The equation is undefined at $\\theta=\\frac\\pi4,\\frac{3\\pi}4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1-t}{1+t}&=\\frac{3(1+t)}{1-t}\\\\(1-t)^2&=3(1+t)^2\\\\1-2t+t^2&=3+6t+3t^2\\\\2t^2+8t+2&=0\\\\t^2+4t+1&=0\\\\t&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{12}}{2}=-2\\pm\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\tan\\theta=-2+\\sqrt3$, $\\theta=\\frac{11\\pi}{12}$. For $\\tan\\theta=-2-\\sqrt3$, $\\theta=\\frac{7\\pi}{12}$.\n\nThe substitution excludes $\\theta=\\frac\\pi2$; substituting gives $-1\\ne-3$, so it is not a solution.\n\nTherefore $\\theta=\\frac{7\\pi}{12}$ or $\\frac{11\\pi}{12}$."
         },
         "questionDiagrams": []
        },
        {
         "id": "v2-1cf69-p14-practice-slot-3-124656-slot-3-q-b",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "b",
         "prompt": "$\\tan\\left(\\theta+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)+\\tan\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)=2\\sqrt3$",
         "answerSpaceMm": 90,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$",
          "worked": "Let $t=\\tan\\theta$. The equation is undefined at $\\theta=\\frac\\pi4,\\frac{3\\pi}4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1+t}{1-t}+\\frac{t-1}{1+t}&=2\\sqrt3\\\\\\frac{(1+t)^2-(1-t)^2}{(1-t)(1+t)}&=2\\sqrt3\\\\\\frac{4t}{1-t^2}&=2\\sqrt3\\\\4t&=2\\sqrt3-2\\sqrt3t^2\\\\\\sqrt3t^2+2t-\\sqrt3&=0\\\\t&=\\frac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{4+12}}{2\\sqrt3}=\\frac{-2\\pm4}{2\\sqrt3}\\\\t&=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\ \\text{or}\\ -\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\tan\\theta=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}$, $\\theta=\\frac\\pi6$. For $\\tan\\theta=-\\sqrt3$, $\\theta=\\frac{2\\pi}3$.\n\nThe substitution excludes $\\theta=\\frac\\pi2$; substituting gives $-1+1=0\\ne2\\sqrt3$, so it is not a solution.\n\nTherefore $\\theta=\\frac\\pi6$ or $\\frac{2\\pi}3$."
         },
         "questionDiagrams": []
        }
