       "content": {
        "id": "v2-proposal-j5-124656-root",
        "type": "question",
        "label": null,
        "prompt": "Solve each equation, for $0\\leq x\\leq2\\pi$, by writing the left side as $R\\sin(x+\\alpha)$.",
        "children": [
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j5-124656-j5-gp-a",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "$\\sqrt3\\sin x+\\cos x=\\sqrt3$",
          "answerSpaceMm": 60,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ or $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$.",
           "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}R\\cos\\alpha&=\\sqrt3\\\\R\\sin\\alpha&=1\\\\R^2&=3+1=4\\\\R&=2\\\\\\tan\\alpha&=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\end{align*}$$\nBoth $\\cos\\alpha$ and $\\sin\\alpha$ are positive, so $\\alpha=\\frac\\pi6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin\\left(x+\\frac\\pi6\\right)&=\\sqrt3\\\\\\sin\\left(x+\\frac\\pi6\\right)&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe transformed domain is $\\frac\\pi6\\leq x+\\frac\\pi6\\leq\\frac{13\\pi}{6}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+\\frac\\pi6&=\\frac\\pi3,\\ \\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\\\x&=\\frac\\pi6,\\ \\frac\\pi2\\end{align*}$$"
          }
         },
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j5-124656-j5-gp-b",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "$\\sin x+\\cos x=-1$",
          "answerSpaceMm": 60,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$x=\\pi$ or $\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$.",
           "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}R\\cos\\alpha&=1\\\\R\\sin\\alpha&=1\\\\R^2&=1+1=2\\\\R&=\\sqrt2\\\\\\tan\\alpha&=1\\end{align*}$$\nBoth are positive, so $\\alpha=\\frac\\pi4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt2\\sin\\left(x+\\frac\\pi4\\right)&=-1\\\\\\sin\\left(x+\\frac\\pi4\\right)&=-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe transformed domain is $\\frac\\pi4\\leq x+\\frac\\pi4\\leq\\frac{9\\pi}{4}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+\\frac\\pi4&=\\frac{5\\pi}{4},\\ \\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\\\x&=\\pi,\\ \\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\end{align*}$$"
          }
         },
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j5-124656-j5-gp-c",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "$\\sin x-\\cos x=\\sqrt2$",
          "answerSpaceMm": 60,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$x=\\frac{3\\pi}{4}$.",
           "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}R\\cos\\alpha&=1\\\\R\\sin\\alpha&=-1\\\\R^2&=1+1=2\\\\R&=\\sqrt2\\\\\\tan\\alpha&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\cos\\alpha>0$ and $\\sin\\alpha<0$, $\\alpha$ is in quadrant IV, so $\\alpha=\\frac{7\\pi}{4}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt2\\sin\\left(x+\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)&=\\sqrt2\\\\\\sin\\left(x+\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThe transformed domain is $\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\leq x+\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\leq\\frac{15\\pi}{4}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+\\frac{7\\pi}{4}&=\\frac{5\\pi}{2}\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\end{align*}$$"
          }
         }
        ],
